1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,008
[laughs] Really?

2
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:11,719
[Chien-yuan] Damn! Yeah.

3
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,971
Kneeling down?

4
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:16,182
- Right.
- Like this?

5
00:00:16,183 --> 00:00:18,519
- Kneeling down like this?
- Yeah.

6
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:20,020
Like this?

7
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,313
- Yeah.
- Cool!

8
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:23,147
[laughing]

9
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:25,692
Your dad really has your back.

10
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:27,778
Of course,
what else would he do?

11
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:29,570
But listen.

12
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:31,698
You need to teach
an ill-behaved dog a lesson.

13
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:33,033
Right?

14
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:34,534
Right.

15
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:35,786
Totally agree.

16
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,245
- Agree?
- Yeah.

17
00:00:37,246 --> 00:00:38,413
- Here.
- Damn!

18
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:41,542
[groans]

19
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:46,046
So, the death
of Chou Lu-yung's dad

20
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:49,007
was a lesson
you taught him, right?

21
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:50,759
- [car horn blowing]
- Pull over!

22
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:55,055
[dramatic music playing]

23
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,265
Right?

24
00:00:57,307 --> 00:00:59,184
- What?
- Huh?

25
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,769
[stammers]

26
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,646
Don't play dumb.

27
00:01:03,647 --> 00:01:06,190
It's almost the end
of the story.
Don't be a buzzkill.

28
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:07,818
Come on. What?

29
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:10,278
What do you want?

30
00:01:10,279 --> 00:01:11,655
It was an accident.

31
00:01:15,284 --> 00:01:16,660
An accident, for real?

32
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,122
- [tire screeching]
- [car horn blowing]

33
00:01:23,542 --> 00:01:24,835
Hmm?

34
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,587
Don't give me
that freaking look.

35
00:01:27,588 --> 00:01:28,754
Come on. What? Tell me.

36
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,382
Fine.

37
00:01:31,717 --> 00:01:35,679
Anyway, back then,
I drove to go after him.

38
00:01:37,681 --> 00:01:41,225
I was right up on his tail,
and he hit the guardrail.

39
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:44,228
He flew over
and crashed down the riverbank.

40
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,314
And Chou Chin-lai...

41
00:01:46,565 --> 00:01:48,566
[mumbles]

42
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:51,819
- What?
- He died!

43
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:55,574
- For real?
- Yeah. Don't you get it?

44
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,580
It was all just fate.

45
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:02,789
Simple as that.

46
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:10,589
So, you got yourself
a scapegoat?

47
00:02:12,341 --> 00:02:13,884
No.

48
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:16,261
I wanted to give him a chance
to prove his worth.

49
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,687
I'll drink this one up.

50
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:27,773
Amazing.

51
00:02:29,441 --> 00:02:32,235
- The police never
found the truth?
- The police?

52
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:34,863
Who am I?

53
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:36,782
Hmm?

54
00:02:36,907 --> 00:02:39,575
The heir of Chang Xin!

55
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:42,120
You know, when the police
saw the name "Chang Xin",

56
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:44,372
they were terrified
like puppies.

57
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:46,458
Puppies? Really?

58
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:48,960
[imitates puppy noises]

59
00:02:54,508 --> 00:02:56,509
[laughing]

60
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:57,635
That crazy?

61
00:02:57,636 --> 00:02:59,720
That's just how it is.

62
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:04,226
Some people are born
to be noble, while some
are born to be low.

63
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:10,564
The law was never meant
to protect the poor.

64
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,859
And these people never get that.

65
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:17,780
[laughs]

66
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:22,702
You're right. I still have
a lot to learn from you.

67
00:03:22,703 --> 00:03:25,330
I'll get this one.
I'll drink it.

68
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:26,540
I'm lucky.

69
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:33,337
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

70
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:37,884
[singing in Mandarin]

71
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:40,220
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

72
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:42,430
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

73
00:03:42,431 --> 00:03:44,557
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

74
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:46,560
[singing in Mandarin]

75
00:03:46,685 --> 00:03:50,730
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

76
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:53,567
[singing in Mandarin]

77
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,535
[Secretary Chin] Sir,

78
00:04:04,411 --> 00:04:06,538
Chien-yuan gave his statement
according to the information

79
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:07,873
Attorney Yang had prepared.

80
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:11,209
The audio file won't be used
as evidence for now.

81
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:13,878
Even if they have
the officer's confession,

82
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,755
it will be considered
insufficient evidence

83
00:04:15,756 --> 00:04:17,465
and not legally effective.

84
00:04:17,466 --> 00:04:19,885
Our attorney is confident
that we won't be prosecuted,

85
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:21,803
and they'll never
re-investigate the case.

86
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:25,640
[sighs]

87
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:27,851
[Chien-yuan shudders]

88
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:30,562
That's great.

89
00:04:32,481 --> 00:04:33,565
Dad,

90
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:35,525
we're fine.

91
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,611
What's so great?

92
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:43,407
Do you know how much
our stock price has plummeted?

93
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:44,742
Huh?

94
00:04:44,743 --> 00:04:46,786
Five percent last month.

95
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:48,330
Ten percent this month.

96
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:51,583
Do you know
how much money we've lost?

97
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,795
I didn't mean it, Dad.

98
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,505
I didn't know it'd be recorded.

99
00:04:57,506 --> 00:05:00,425
What do you know then, huh?

100
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:08,600
I'm not sure
if you're naive or stupid.

101
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:10,936
[grunts]

102
00:05:11,937 --> 00:05:13,396
[groans]

103
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:22,322
You'll drag Chang Xin down
sooner or later.

104
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:29,913
[sighs]

105
00:05:39,548 --> 00:05:40,632
Dad?

106
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:44,636
It's my fault.

107
00:05:45,679 --> 00:05:46,805
I'll deal with it.

108
00:05:48,557 --> 00:05:50,016
I won't ruin your reputation.

109
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:52,602
What are you planning to do?

110
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:55,062
[tense music playing]

111
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,356
How can you deal with it?

112
00:05:57,816 --> 00:05:59,693
Tell me! What do we do?

113
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:04,655
You wouldn't have been recorded
if you were capable.

114
00:06:04,656 --> 00:06:05,782
Deal with it?

115
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:10,161
[sighs]

116
00:06:24,843 --> 00:06:26,094
Listen up.

117
00:06:27,846 --> 00:06:30,807
Someone is digging a hole
for the two of us to fall into,

118
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:34,060
trying to take us both down.

119
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:35,770
So, from now on,

120
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:39,941
you'll stay home
and do nothing at all.

121
00:06:41,401 --> 00:06:43,611
I'll deal with everything.

122
00:06:43,612 --> 00:06:45,030
Understand?

123
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:47,741
Yes.

124
00:06:51,578 --> 00:06:52,704
Go home.

125
00:07:15,727 --> 00:07:16,977
Secretary Chin?

126
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,063
Yes?

127
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:22,776
I want to know

128
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:26,071
who did this to us.

129
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:28,907
Yes, sir.

130
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:31,201
Consider it done.

131
00:07:38,041 --> 00:07:41,628
[Chen] Just as we expected,
he just can't let go.

132
00:07:43,922 --> 00:07:46,591
He's his own flesh and blood.
It's really difficult.

133
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:48,634
[shareholder 1]
Chang Da-chin refuses

134
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:50,929
to cut ties with his son,
which is why
the shareholders are wavering.

135
00:07:51,054 --> 00:07:53,807
When are you
going to do something?

136
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:55,557
[shareholder 2] Yeah.

137
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:58,770
The troubles his son causes
get bigger and bigger each time.

138
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:00,604
Chairman Chang
isn't fit to lead anymore.

139
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,648
[shareholder 2] The Chairman
only has deep enough pockets

140
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:04,150
to take the hits from his son
again and again.

141
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:06,069
[dramatic music playing]

142
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:09,154
Shu-min, you need to step up.

143
00:08:09,155 --> 00:08:11,031
We're all with you.

144
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:13,618
Director Chiang, don't hesitate.

145
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:15,077
Fight against him now.

146
00:08:15,078 --> 00:08:16,954
You're the second
largest shareholder.

147
00:08:16,955 --> 00:08:19,707
If you don't do something,
nobody will.

148
00:08:19,708 --> 00:08:21,625
Have you thought about calling
an extraordinary general meeting

149
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,628
to dethrone Chairman Chang?

150
00:08:29,968 --> 00:08:32,137
Here's what I think.

151
00:08:32,262 --> 00:08:34,723
Everything has
a stop-loss point.

152
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,734
It's not yet time.

153
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:50,655
When do you think it's time?

154
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:54,826
With public outrage
boiling over,

155
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:56,869
if we do things hastily,

156
00:08:56,870 --> 00:09:00,832
Chairman Chang will use
all his power to make sure
we never rise again.

157
00:09:06,921 --> 00:09:08,298
Unless...

158
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:15,722
Chien-yuan's hit-and-run case
is re-investigated.

159
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:17,599
[music intensifies]

160
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:23,021
If they re-investigate the case,
you'll get ready to attack?

161
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:26,066
- On one condition.
- What is it?

162
00:09:29,861 --> 00:09:33,281
He continues to protect his son,
not cutting ties.

163
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:43,917
Sir, to stop any more losses,

164
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:46,711
you need to fire Chien-yuan.

165
00:09:48,338 --> 00:09:50,214
Don't worry.

166
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:52,592
Legally, we'll be fine.

167
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,718
It's not a legal matter.

168
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:57,222
The public will boycott
Chang Xin soon.

169
00:09:57,347 --> 00:09:59,599
All our subsidiaries
will be dragged into this.

170
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,768
Our stock price will plummet.

171
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:03,727
[laughs]

172
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:08,732
Shu-min,
I've been through so much.

173
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,235
But I'm fine now, right?

174
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,861
Huh?

175
00:10:12,904 --> 00:10:16,282
Ten years ago,
he was a high school student.

176
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:19,785
Could he deal
with something like that?

177
00:10:19,786 --> 00:10:23,330
If the hit-and-run case
is re-investigated,

178
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:25,834
do you think
they won't suspect you?

179
00:10:28,878 --> 00:10:31,755
Chien-yuan won't be
the only one in trouble.

180
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,633
The public will point
their fingers at you as well.

181
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:35,885
[dramatic music playing]

182
00:10:38,096 --> 00:10:39,931
[sighs]

183
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:43,268
[exhales]

184
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,396
Shu-min,

185
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:48,898
stop wasting your breath.

186
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:53,444
Even if he's a good-for-nothing,
Chien-yuan is still my son.

187
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:57,782
I'll never, ever give him up.

188
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:01,286
I think I've made my point, right?

189
00:11:03,288 --> 00:11:05,956
[doorbell rings]

190
00:11:05,957 --> 00:11:08,835
- Yeah?
- [dog barking]

191
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:18,428
What you're here
to say is no different
from last time, right?

192
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:22,849
But the situation
is different now.

193
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:24,976
You've seen the news, I reckon?

194
00:11:26,269 --> 00:11:29,229
Everybody knows about
Chang Chien-yuan's confession.

195
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,315
With your help, Mr. Wang,

196
00:11:31,316 --> 00:11:34,402
it's very likely
we can throw both Chang Da-chin
and his son into jail.

197
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:41,492
I'm sorry that
you made the trip for nothing.

198
00:11:46,122 --> 00:11:48,833
I was about to go out
to testify to the case.

199
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:53,087
[triumphant music playing]

200
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:07,893
That's the driver,
Chang Chien-yuan's scapegoat.

201
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:10,187
[Officer Wang] When your dad
had the car accident,

202
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:11,522
the security camera
of a seafood restaurant

203
00:12:11,773 --> 00:12:13,815
showed this guy
eating and drinking there.

204
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:16,194
He couldn't possibly be
the hit-and-run driver.

205
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:21,199
With this, the case is very
likely to be re-investigated.

206
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:23,326
Yeah.

207
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,373
Chief!

208
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:29,791
Chief?

209
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:33,753
We've got the wrong guy.

210
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:44,764
Everything else was burned.

211
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:47,267
I kept this sheet in secret.

212
00:12:51,062 --> 00:12:54,107
I'm planning
to turn myself in with it.

213
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:03,073
<i>The next story
is about the hit-and-run
scandal involving</i>

214
00:13:03,074 --> 00:13:05,242
<i>Chang Xin's heir,
Chang Chien-yuan.</i>

215
00:13:05,243 --> 00:13:09,455
<i>A retired police officer
named Wang, who was in charge
of the investigation,</i>

216
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,416
<i>has stepped forward to testify
that the driver in jail</i>

217
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:15,210
<i>actually had an alibi.</i>

218
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:18,255
<i>He claimed that
his superiors forced him
to conceal the case.</i>

219
00:13:18,256 --> 00:13:23,093
<i>Prosecutors have indicated
that the case is very likely
to be re-investigated.</i>

220
00:13:23,094 --> 00:13:24,929
[cheers]

221
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:31,018
If that's true,
Officer Wang committed a crime.

222
00:13:31,019 --> 00:13:32,227
Perjury.

223
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:33,938
Was it worth it?

224
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:36,941
It's better late than never.
That's a real man. I admire him.

225
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:40,277
Then the prosecutors
may find out the truth.

226
00:13:40,278 --> 00:13:41,987
- And...
- And Chang Da-chin

227
00:13:41,988 --> 00:13:43,990
will be put in jail
with his good-for-nothing son.

228
00:13:44,115 --> 00:13:45,908
- Great.
- Great.

229
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:49,120
The law is all about evidence.

230
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:51,789
Without evidence,
nothing will happen.

231
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:55,334
As long as Chang Da-chin
plays dumb, you can't do
anything to him.

232
00:13:55,335 --> 00:13:57,419
Do you think
the prosecutors would believe

233
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:00,798
an 18-year-old high school kid
could find himself a scapegoat?

234
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:02,507
[Feng] An 18-year-old
isn't a kid.

235
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:04,217
He's old enough to get married
and have a child.

236
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:05,845
That has nothing
to do with this.

237
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:07,013
[Feng] Hmm...

238
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:09,181
But to make Chang
Chien-yuan his heir,

239
00:14:09,182 --> 00:14:11,308
Chang Da-chin has cleaned up
all his messes.

240
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:13,144
I don't think
he would give him up.

241
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:17,064
Anyway, Chang Da-chin
will be in jail. It'll be
the end of Chang Xin.

242
00:14:17,065 --> 00:14:21,486
By then, Jin Lai Hao will be
number one in Taiwan.

243
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:22,986
- Number one in Taiwan.
- Come on.

244
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:24,405
- Taiwan...
- That's enough.

245
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:26,908
I'm sorry.

246
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:33,331
[dramatic music playing]

247
00:14:40,171 --> 00:14:43,216
[cell phone vibrating]

248
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:49,639
Hello?

249
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:55,060
Okay.

250
00:14:55,061 --> 00:14:58,106
[music intensifies]

251
00:15:09,117 --> 00:15:11,535
[Secretary Chin]
Thank you all for coming.

252
00:15:11,536 --> 00:15:14,539
Thank you for your long-term
support and attention
to Chang Xin Group.

253
00:15:14,664 --> 00:15:18,250
- Chairman Chang Da-chin called
this press conference today...
- What happened?

254
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:20,627
...to make an announcement
to the public.

255
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:21,921
- At short notice.
- Please welcome...

256
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,588
- Chairman Chang Da-chin.
- I have no idea.

257
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,299
[camera shutters]

258
00:15:30,555 --> 00:15:32,431
[Chang Ta-chin]
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

259
00:15:32,432 --> 00:15:33,599
LIVE: PRESS CONFERENCE

260
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:35,685
<i>I'm here today
to represent both Chang Xin</i>

261
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:40,647
and the Chang family
to tell you that...

262
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:44,569
my son is under investigation
for a hit-and-run case.

263
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:47,447
According to our attorney,

264
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:50,575
based on the lack of evidence
and other circumstances,

265
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:54,245
they can't prove
that he was involved.

266
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:59,959
So, my son is likely
to be found not guilty.

267
00:16:06,257 --> 00:16:08,133
[camera shutters continue]

268
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:11,179
[soft dramatic music playing]

269
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:24,275
But not long ago,

270
00:16:27,487 --> 00:16:29,989
when my son came back
from the police station,

271
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:37,288
he told me personally that

272
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:44,629
the fatal car accident
ten years ago

273
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:51,135
was caused by him.

274
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:01,771
With my money,

275
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:03,356
he got himself

276
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,650
a scapegoat.

277
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:08,653
What the hell?

278
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:12,697
[Chang Ta-chin] <i>I couldn't
believe it, so I looked
into the whole thing.</i>

279
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,741
Trying to get away with it.

280
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:17,203
Good job. Bravo.

281
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:21,123
[Chang Ta-chin]
<i>I am shocked and guilty.</i>

282
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:26,629
It's all my fault.

283
00:17:31,634 --> 00:17:33,803
I had been
so focused on my career

284
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,680
that I didn't teach my son well.

285
00:17:38,349 --> 00:17:40,726
However, he did something
so lawless...

286
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,065
and even hid it from me.

287
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:50,194
As his father,

288
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:53,739
the least I can do

289
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:03,540
is to personally hand him over
to the police.

290
00:18:03,541 --> 00:18:05,626
[music intensifies]

291
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:21,684
He must pay the price
for the crime he has committed.

292
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:26,731
I hereby announce
Chang Chien-yuan is removed
from his position.

293
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:35,156
Effective immediately.

294
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:43,663
To the victim

295
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:46,459
killed by my son,

296
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:47,710
Mr. Chou Chin-lai,

297
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,130
<i>and his family,</i>

298
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:55,592
I offer my deepest,
deepest apologies.

299
00:18:55,593 --> 00:18:56,761
Damn!

300
00:18:57,845 --> 00:18:59,430
I will atone

301
00:19:01,349 --> 00:19:02,767
for the rest of my life.

302
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:16,321
Is that your box of cigarettes?

303
00:19:16,322 --> 00:19:18,949
[music continues]

304
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,215
So, I'll take
all the responsibility.

305
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:20,845
Chien-yuan,

306
00:20:23,681 --> 00:20:25,725
I did this for your sake.

307
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:28,894
I'm holding onto Chang Xin

308
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:31,604
to promise you a better future.
Understand?

309
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:33,565
[soft dramatic music playing]

310
00:20:33,566 --> 00:20:34,984
- [scoffs]
- [police sirens]

311
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:58,340
Take care of yourself.

312
00:22:02,905 --> 00:22:05,074
Excuse me, Catherine.
The Chairman is here.

313
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:08,410
[tense music playing]

314
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:22,675
[Chang Ta-chin]
I'm here to thank you.

315
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:26,762
Thank you for your
valuable opinions.

316
00:22:28,389 --> 00:22:30,015
I thought about it afterward

317
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,851
and realized I needed
to cut ties.

318
00:22:33,394 --> 00:22:35,479
I know it was
a dilemma for you, sir.

319
00:22:35,604 --> 00:22:37,481
It wasn't easy
to make the choice.

320
00:22:38,649 --> 00:22:39,984
Right.

321
00:22:40,109 --> 00:22:41,527
It was indeed.

322
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:44,989
But I had no choice.

323
00:22:45,114 --> 00:22:48,032
He is my own son,

324
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:50,744
and I had to hold
a press conference.

325
00:22:52,162 --> 00:22:53,831
[sighs]

326
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:55,040
Forget it.

327
00:22:57,418 --> 00:22:59,003
[soft chuckles]

328
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:01,088
We do everything
for Chang Xin's benefit.

329
00:23:05,759 --> 00:23:06,844
Yeah,

330
00:23:07,970 --> 00:23:09,471
for Chang Xin's benefit.

331
00:23:10,598 --> 00:23:12,515
[sighs]

332
00:23:12,516 --> 00:23:15,894
Just like you tried to call
a shareholders' meeting
to get me replaced.

333
00:23:15,895 --> 00:23:17,438
That was for
Chang Xin's benefit.

334
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:24,570
Like you said,

335
00:23:24,695 --> 00:23:26,530
for Chang Xin's benefit,

336
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:28,407
I won't hold that against you.

337
00:23:31,452 --> 00:23:34,872
But I have something else
to ask you.

338
00:23:38,918 --> 00:23:41,794
You arranged for your own man
to be around my son.

339
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,672
Also for Chang Xin's benefit?

340
00:23:47,176 --> 00:23:48,844
I don't get it.

341
00:23:50,930 --> 00:23:52,889
[chuckles]

342
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:54,892
Fine. That's not important.

343
00:23:58,729 --> 00:23:59,813
Director Chiang,

344
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:03,733
I'm sorry.

345
00:24:03,734 --> 00:24:04,860
I...

346
00:24:05,903 --> 00:24:07,738
I've done it
for Chang Xin's benefit.

347
00:24:13,452 --> 00:24:14,995
[sighs]

348
00:24:17,081 --> 00:24:19,083
Being betrayed by your own man

349
00:24:19,208 --> 00:24:21,543
is a terrible feeling.

350
00:24:25,965 --> 00:24:27,591
But don't worry.

351
00:24:27,716 --> 00:24:29,926
For your dad's sake,

352
00:24:29,927 --> 00:24:33,013
I won't do anything
to the company he left you.

353
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:39,103
But I'm going to remove you
from all positions at Chang Xin.

354
00:24:44,942 --> 00:24:47,861
If you're still able
to call a shareholders' meeting,

355
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:51,115
bring it on.

356
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:52,616
Huh?

357
00:25:10,259 --> 00:25:12,136
The defendant, Chang Chien-yuan,

358
00:25:12,261 --> 00:25:16,807
for negligent homicide
under Article 276
of the Criminal Code,

359
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:20,811
is sentenced to four years
and seven months in prison.

360
00:25:20,936 --> 00:25:24,981
As for hit-and-run
under Article 185-4,

361
00:25:24,982 --> 00:25:28,735
he's sentenced to four years
and three months in prison.

362
00:25:28,736 --> 00:25:33,197
The total combined sentence
is eight years and ten months.

363
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:34,324
Court is adjourned.

364
00:25:34,575 --> 00:25:37,828
[dramatic music playing]

365
00:26:20,788 --> 00:26:23,040
You're feeling good
right now, I reckon?

366
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:26,210
[scoffs] No, I'm not.

367
00:26:26,877 --> 00:26:29,879
With you sitting here safe
and sound, I'm not feeling good.

368
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:31,924
[chuckles]

369
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:38,222
I won't let you
get away with this.

370
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:41,850
Me neither.

371
00:27:06,166 --> 00:27:08,085
- [Chang Ta-chin] Hsiu-wen?
- [Hsiu-wen] Yes, sir.

372
00:27:08,836 --> 00:27:13,215
While Chien-yuan is absent,
you'll take over his job.

373
00:27:14,925 --> 00:27:16,926
You'll have greater power,

374
00:27:16,927 --> 00:27:19,763
but correspondingly,
you'll take on more
responsibilities.

375
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:22,306
Can you do that?

376
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:24,226
Yes, sir. Thank you, sir.

377
00:27:25,978 --> 00:27:30,148
Let's see how much
higher you can climb.

378
00:27:30,149 --> 00:27:31,275
Yes, sir.

379
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:37,072
By the way, tell me.

380
00:27:38,157 --> 00:27:41,200
Has the person
Chou Lu-yung cares about most

381
00:27:41,201 --> 00:27:43,661
become another girl now?

382
00:27:43,662 --> 00:27:45,414
[uneasy music playing]

383
00:27:50,294 --> 00:27:54,089
Do you mean Chao Yi-hsuan?

384
00:27:58,343 --> 00:28:00,470
[chuckles] It's alright.

385
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:03,891
I'm just asking.
Don't take it to heart.

386
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:11,315
[soft thunder]

387
00:28:35,464 --> 00:28:36,840
Thanks for coming.

388
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:43,013
You're welcome.

389
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:45,724
I'm here because I want to be.

390
00:28:56,944 --> 00:28:59,363
IN LOVING MEMORY
OF CHOU CHIN-LAI

391
00:29:01,990 --> 00:29:03,325
I've got to go, Uncle.

392
00:29:05,035 --> 00:29:06,161
Bye.

393
00:29:11,333 --> 00:29:14,378
[soft dramatic music playing]

394
00:29:30,978 --> 00:29:32,062
Dad,

395
00:29:33,230 --> 00:29:34,314
how are you?

396
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:43,490
I have a bunch of great friends
taking care of me.

397
00:29:45,242 --> 00:29:46,368
Don't worry.

398
00:29:52,416 --> 00:29:53,959
I'm becoming more
and more like you.

399
00:29:55,294 --> 00:29:57,212
I can make all your dishes

400
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:00,799
and run a restaurant.

401
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:06,054
I can take care of those
around me, just like you.

402
00:30:17,441 --> 00:30:19,484
Start with the end in mind,

403
00:30:19,609 --> 00:30:21,194
hold on to our beliefs.

404
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,033
Dad,

405
00:30:27,284 --> 00:30:29,453
you're everything I believe in.

406
00:30:38,295 --> 00:30:39,463
To you.

407
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:02,152
I miss you.

408
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:12,996
[Chang Ta-chin]
<i>By the way, tell me.</i>

409
00:31:13,914 --> 00:31:17,042
Has the person
Chou Lu-yung cares about most

410
00:31:17,167 --> 00:31:19,336
become another girl now?

411
00:31:20,003 --> 00:31:22,047
[thunder rumbling]

412
00:31:33,642 --> 00:31:35,644
[music continues]

413
00:31:38,438 --> 00:31:40,023
Did you drive here?

414
00:31:44,903 --> 00:31:46,154
I'll give you a ride.

415
00:31:49,658 --> 00:31:50,951
Okay.

416
00:32:14,975 --> 00:32:16,518
Please, Miss Chao.

417
00:32:17,561 --> 00:32:19,563
[energetic music playing]

418
00:32:29,239 --> 00:32:30,449
This way, Miss Chao.

419
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:36,580
[Chang Ta-chin] I love meeting

420
00:32:37,289 --> 00:32:39,583
talented and promising
young people.

421
00:32:42,711 --> 00:32:45,589
Then you should
meet me indeed, sir.

422
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:47,757
[laughs] Hmm.

423
00:32:50,093 --> 00:32:51,595
Do you want to work
for Chang Xin?

424
00:32:57,684 --> 00:32:59,686
I think you're talented.

425
00:33:00,729 --> 00:33:05,442
A promising young lady
should work
for a larger company.

426
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:10,280
Sir, rather than working
for a large company,

427
00:33:10,405 --> 00:33:12,449
I enjoy making a company larger.

428
00:33:14,075 --> 00:33:15,368
Oh...

429
00:33:16,620 --> 00:33:20,040
We give Chang Xin's shares
to our senior executives.

430
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:23,710
I think
I can buy some on my own.

431
00:33:27,547 --> 00:33:28,632
Fine.

432
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:31,426
Tell me.

433
00:33:33,512 --> 00:33:37,724
What is it that Chou Lu-yung
can give you that we can't?

434
00:33:43,188 --> 00:33:44,272
Sir,

435
00:33:47,526 --> 00:33:49,736
I love being on top of men.

436
00:33:53,406 --> 00:33:55,367
[dramatic music playing]

437
00:33:56,284 --> 00:33:58,328
[laughs]

438
00:34:02,290 --> 00:34:07,337
Girl, I love spirited
and vigorous young people.

439
00:34:09,339 --> 00:34:10,590
But don't forget

440
00:34:11,675 --> 00:34:15,177
that life can be easy

441
00:34:15,178 --> 00:34:17,347
or difficult.

442
00:34:17,472 --> 00:34:20,058
It depends
on which side you choose.

443
00:34:23,645 --> 00:34:25,564
Thanks for the reminder.

444
00:34:25,689 --> 00:34:28,525
But I love the side I've chosen.

445
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:37,158
A piece of advice for you.

446
00:34:38,326 --> 00:34:39,536
Think about it.

447
00:34:40,537 --> 00:34:44,833
Is Chou Lu-yung
really nice to you, huh?

448
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:47,544
It's simple here.

449
00:34:48,712 --> 00:34:50,297
Ask for anything you want.

450
00:34:52,591 --> 00:34:54,800
Ask for anything I want?

451
00:34:54,801 --> 00:34:55,885
Of course.

452
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:08,273
I think whatever
Chang Xin can give me...

453
00:35:13,403 --> 00:35:16,114
I'm not interested in at all.

454
00:35:18,742 --> 00:35:20,076
Thank you, sir.

455
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:21,453
Bye.

456
00:35:22,912 --> 00:35:24,205
Girl?

457
00:35:29,878 --> 00:35:31,755
Think twice before you go.

458
00:35:32,756 --> 00:35:34,674
You're welcome
to come back here anytime

459
00:35:35,550 --> 00:35:36,593
to have a cup of tea.

460
00:35:36,718 --> 00:35:38,261
[chuckles]

461
00:35:39,304 --> 00:35:40,554
Thank you, sir.

462
00:35:40,555 --> 00:35:41,765
I loved the tea.

463
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:04,454
Thanks for the ride.

464
00:36:06,373 --> 00:36:07,457
You're welcome.

465
00:36:20,637 --> 00:36:21,680
Lu-yung?

466
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:24,349
Hmm?

467
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:31,439
[soft dramatic music playing]

468
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:56,423
I don't think
I've hugged you like this.

469
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:01,678
But this is the last time.

470
00:37:02,846 --> 00:37:04,806
[singer singing in Mandarin]

471
00:37:17,610 --> 00:37:18,862
Chou Lu-yung...

472
00:37:22,449 --> 00:37:23,616
I'm in love with you.

473
00:37:28,496 --> 00:37:30,540
I've been in love
with you all this time.

474
00:37:31,666 --> 00:37:34,711
[singing continues]

475
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:59,402
But we're going separate ways...

476
00:38:03,406 --> 00:38:05,283
with no turning back.

477
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:36,021
When you meet the right person,
cherish her.

478
00:38:36,022 --> 00:38:38,691
As a friend,
this is my best advice for you.

479
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:47,450
Take care.

480
00:39:21,442 --> 00:39:23,152
I don't like poor boys.

481
00:39:23,403 --> 00:39:24,487
From now on,

482
00:39:25,655 --> 00:39:27,532
becoming rich is my goal.

483
00:39:31,578 --> 00:39:32,828
You'll never be my rival.

484
00:39:32,829 --> 00:39:34,831
[singing continues]

485
00:39:57,937 --> 00:39:59,188
Don't fall in love with me.

486
00:40:57,830 --> 00:41:00,833
[suspenseful music playing]

487
00:41:05,713 --> 00:41:08,257
[piano music playing]

488
00:41:10,593 --> 00:41:12,178
Where's the girl's mom?

489
00:41:13,805 --> 00:41:16,598
Gone to a faraway place.
Won't come back again.

490
00:41:16,599 --> 00:41:17,976
[frustrated sighs]

491
00:41:18,101 --> 00:41:20,478
You just can't say
things clearly?

492
00:41:20,603 --> 00:41:22,939
Her mom was my boss' secretary.

493
00:41:23,064 --> 00:41:25,108
She was in trouble
and fled overseas.

494
00:41:25,233 --> 00:41:26,609
Where's her dad?

495
00:41:28,111 --> 00:41:29,779
[Wen] <i>Unknown.</i>

496
00:42:00,059 --> 00:42:01,644
Why are you here?

497
00:42:09,652 --> 00:42:11,821
[thunder rumbling]

498
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:22,957
[faint jazz music playing]

499
00:42:32,008 --> 00:42:33,760
Why did you ask me out here?

500
00:42:45,188 --> 00:42:47,231
You're busy. Must be exhausted.

501
00:42:49,108 --> 00:42:50,276
No, I'm fine.

502
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:54,697
But you look bad.

503
00:42:54,822 --> 00:42:57,200
You need to get some rest.

504
00:42:57,325 --> 00:42:59,160
Stop nagging me.

505
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:01,704
Why don't you go hit on my mom?

506
00:43:02,163 --> 00:43:03,998
Don't waste your time.
You're old enough.

507
00:43:08,086 --> 00:43:09,837
What exactly is it?

508
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:13,049
You've been hesitating
for so long. Want to borrow
some money?

509
00:43:19,305 --> 00:43:22,350
[dramatic music playing]

510
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:43,412
Wen, although age
doesn't matter in love,

511
00:43:43,663 --> 00:43:45,331
I'm not interested
in you at all.

512
00:43:47,959 --> 00:43:51,879
Or do you want me to find out
if my mom is interested in you?

513
00:44:05,059 --> 00:44:07,770
Yi-hsuan, do you remember
the name Ching?

514
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:16,195
Your real mom is Chao Yu-jung.

515
00:44:17,780 --> 00:44:20,283
She had an affair
with Chang Da-chin.

516
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:26,956
Chang Da-chin is your father.

517
00:44:28,291 --> 00:44:31,294
[music intensifies]

518
00:44:41,179 --> 00:44:43,181
[credits music playing]

519
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:53,274
[singer singing in Mandarin]
